<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.plane.reads ~ read one record across the sensorium planes

One `cid` answers its presence and a payload summary across content, structure and form, an honest null where a plane lacks it. `sensorium` names the sensorium; absent, memory.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///sense.plane.reads", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ cid · sensorium

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`cid` params=`takes/word needs/required seat/1 as/<cid> ~ the record's content id`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium` params=`takes/word skins/mcp ~ the sensorium by name; absent, memory (the terminal names it before the verb: lares sense <sensorium> <verb>)`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ cli · mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/cli`>>

!!! lares sense plane-record

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`cli` params=`handler/host spells/[[lares sense plane-record]] ~ the terminal`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! act lar:///sense.plane.reads

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/seat spells/[[act lar:///sense.plane.reads]] ~ the seat runs it in its own process`>>
```

